note vocabulary.txt: the words identifiers may be made of, and the banned synonyms with the word to use instead. It exists so one concept has one name across the code: archlint splits every identifier the code chooses into words and fails on a word that is not listed, or on a synonym with its canonical spelling. An agent may add a word for a new concept; which of two words is canonical is the owner's decision, so the gate fails when a synonym line changes. cargo xtask words lists every unknown or synonym word in strict code with a count and its first place, for sizing a vocabulary change.

